  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Pair the smallest number with the largest. Moving inward increases one number by \\(1\\) and decreases the other by \\(1\\), so each pair has the same sum:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(90+99)+(91+98)+(92+97)\\\\\n&\\qquad +(93+96)+(94+95).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThese five pairs use every number from \\(90\\) through \\(99\\) exactly once. Each pair totals \\(189\\), so the sum is \\(5\\times189=945\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
